# Who has to review what.
#
# A public template is forked, generated from, and contributed to by people who
# have never read `RULES.md`. This file is the backstop for the parts where a
# well-meaning change is expensive: an unreviewed edit to a policy, a hook or a
# workflow is the one that reaches every repository generated from this one.
#
# GitHub only enforces it when the branch rule requires review from code owners.
# Without that rule it is a suggestion; `docs/contributing-security.md` says how
# to turn it on.

# Everything, by default.
*                               @ishakdeveloper

